  "meta": {
    "name": "Valve leak and onset voltage",
    "description": "Valve back-leak and onset voltage. Syringe through the stopcock (closed to waste), syringe EMPTY at the start, Control pressure ticked. Fill: the syringe holds 5 mbar while 600 Hz at 2.5 V runs 90 s. Part A (pump OFF): push to 50, 100 mbar, hold the position with the motor energised for 30 s (back-leak decay through the valves), gentle release. Part B: 600 Hz at 0.5, 0.6, 0.7, 0.8, 0.9, 1, 2.5 V, 20 s each with 15 s zeros, syringe holding ~5 mbar (near free flow); 0.5 V may draw no current (expected); below 0.8 V cross-check the PPK2 with supply/supply.csv. Type the Pump ID. Open the stopcock to waste before ANY manual syringe push.",
